==Trivia==
*With sequences and variations of those sequences for every alien and alien enhancement, the '''[[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]]''' has the most transformation sequences out of any other show in the [[Ben 10 (Franchise)|franchise]], coming in at around 214.
*Some sequences in later shows pay homage to those of the past:
**Classic aliens like [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]] and [[Wildmutt]] have their standard sequences from the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' referenced in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''.
**The episode ''[[Alien X-Tinction]]'' showcased Reboot-style transformations that paid homage to the sequences of the '''Original Series''' and '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''.
*A joke{{Refn|[[:File:Tim Buk TV OS theme gag details.PNG]]|group = AL}} in ''[[Tim Buk-TV]]'' suggests that [[Ben Tennyson (Reboot)|Ben]]'s transformation sequences all happen in his head, and are seemingly unimpressive to an outside observer.
*The macabre nature of the transformations in the '''Original Series''' were intentional. They were meant to look painful for the user.{{Refn|[[:File:Classic Transformation Sequences Painful.PNG]]|group = DR}}
**Despite this, [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] testifies that he doesn't feel much pain from transforming; he equates them to feeling "like a...good stretch".<ref>''[[Bros in Space]]''</ref><ref>[[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Tennyson]]</ref>

